  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinCare 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Your wife is participating in a clinical trial that follows a strict
    medication schedule. One evening, you notice that she forgot a dose. You remind
    her to take her medicine and help her record the late dose and her symptoms in
    her trial diary.\n\n<b>Which of the following best describes the caregiver\u2019s
    role in this situation?</b>"
  explanation: Caregivers play an important supportive role by helping patients manage
    treatment schedules and track symptoms, ensuring accurate data collection and
    reducing stress for the patient. By staying organized and attentive, caregivers
    help patients keep up with complex routines and communicate key information to
    help the trial reach its goals. This partnership between patients and caregivers
    helps researchers get the most reliable information while keeping participation
    as manageable as possible.
  correctAnswer: Providing essential logistical and emotional support to the patient
    to help maintain trial accuracy.
  incorrectAnswer1: "Limiting their involvement in the patient\u2019s treatment plan
    to avoid influencing trial data."
  incorrectAnswer2: Acting as a substitute researcher for the trial.
  incorrectAnswer3: "Overstepping\u2014only the research team should track the patient\u2019s
    ability to follow the treatment plan. "
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
